I can't reliably quote Shabbat 96b:11 word-for-word. Segment numbers like ":11" follow Sefaria's divisions, and I can't verify which exact line falls at that position, so anything I gave you might be wrong or invented.

In general, Shabbat 96b covers:
- the end of the discussion of carrying (passing objects) between domains;
- the baraita identifying the wood-gatherer (*mekoshesh*) of Numbers 15 as Tzelofchad (Rabbi Akiva's view);
- Rabbi Yehuda ben Beteira's rebuke of Rabbi Akiva for revealing this.

For the exact text of segment 11, check sefaria.org/Shabbat.96b.11 directly.
